# kitchenowl-cli

Command-line client for KitchenOwl's `/api` endpoints, focused on recipe workflows.

## Features

- JWT login with refresh-token rotation support.
- Config storage in `~/.config/kitchenowl/config.json`.
- Household listing and default household selection.
- Recipe basics:
  - list recipes
  - get recipe details
  - add recipes
  - edit recipes
  - delete recipes
- Script-friendly `--json` output and YAML/JSON file payload support.

## Install (local)

```bash
cd /Users/andreas/Documents/code/kitchenowl/kitchenowl-cli
python3 -m pip install -e .
```

## Quick start

```bash
kitchenowl auth login --server https://your-kitchenowl.example.com
kitchenowl household list
kitchenowl household use 1
kitchenowl recipe list
kitchenowl recipe get 42
kitchenowl recipe add --name "Tomato Soup" --description "Simple soup" --yields 2 --time 25
kitchenowl recipe edit 42
kitchenowl recipe delete 42
```

## File-based create/edit

```bash
kitchenowl recipe add --household-id 1 --from-file recipe.yml
kitchenowl recipe edit 42 --from-file recipe.yml
```

Example `recipe.yml`:

```yaml
name: Tomato Soup
description: Simple soup
time: 25
cook_time: 20
prep_time: 5
yields: 2
visibility: 0
source: ""
items:
  - name: Tomatoes
    description: 6 pcs
    optional: false
  - name: Salt
    description: 1 tsp
    optional: false
tags:
  - soup
  - vegetarian
```
